{
 "_doc": "What the Trainer Notebook's media/<exercise id> docs hold. Pictures: Everkinetic drawings (github.com/everkinetic/data, CC BY-SA 4.0; dist/svg/<id_num>-relaxation|tension.svg; `everkinetic` = id_num) uploaded to the artifact's asset store (asset_id -> /_blob/<id>), two Wikimedia Commons files with their own licence. A near-match drawing carries `fit_note`; push-ups, dips and squats show Top (tension file) before Bottom; plank holds show the push-up top only. Pre-loaded 2026-11-24 (18 exercises) and 2026-11-25 (26 more, each drawing looked at before attaching). Videos: YouTube links verified live via oEmbed (title + channel). Excluded on purpose: barbell hack squat, free-standing T-bar row, behind-the-neck pulldown, barbell overhead squat (catalog never list), the seated cable row drawing for the chest-supported row machine (teaches the unsupported position) and a strict one-arm press for the push press (no leg drive). Alex's own photos (added_by: me, role: machine | placard) live only in the artifact's db.",
